theory.intro:
The **average rate of change** of $y = f(x)$ over $[a, b]$ is how much $y$ changes per unit of $x$ on average. It is the gradient of the **secant**, the straight line through $(a, f(a))$ and $(b, f(b))$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.3:5.0,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.18*\x*\x + 0.4}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (1.2,0.6592) -- (4.3,0.6592) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$\Delta x$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (4.3,0.6592) -- (4.3,3.7282) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$\Delta y$};
\draw[thick,red] (0.8,0.2632) -- (4.8,4.2232) node[right,font=\small] {secant};
\fill (1.2,0.6592) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (4.3,3.7282) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\small] at (1.2,0.6592) {$(a,f(a))$};
\node[above left,font=\small] at (4.3,3.7282) {$(b,f(b))$};
\draw (1.2,0) -- (1.2,-0.12) node[below] {$a$};
\draw (4.3,0) -- (4.3,-0.12) node[below] {$b$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The graph of $y = f(x)$ shows a secant line joining $(1, 2)$ and $(5, 14)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/3,2/6,3/9,4/12,5/15} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue] plot[smooth,tension=0.6] coordinates {(0.5,0.4) (1,0.67) (2,1.33) (3,2.33) (4,3.5) (5,4.67) (5.5,5.3)} node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0.5,0.17) -- (5.5,5.17);
\fill (1,0.67) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (1,0.67) {$(1,2)$};
\fill (5,4.67) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below right,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (5,4.67) {$(5,14)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the gradient of the secant line.

The graph shows the temperature $T$ ($^{\circ}\text{C}$) of a warming liquid over time $t$ (minutes).
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$T$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue] plot[smooth,tension=0.6] coordinates {(0,1) (1,1.8) (2,2.5) (3,3.1) (4,3.6) (5,4.0)} node[above left] {$T(t)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,1) -- (4,3.6);
\fill (0,1) circle (2.5pt);
\node[right,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (0,1) {$(0,10)$};
\fill (4,3.6) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (4,3.6) {$(4,36)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Temperature ($^{\circ}\text{C}$)};
\node[below] at (3.2,-0.9) {Time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the average rate of temperature increase over the first $4$ minutes.

development.question_text:
The graph of $y = f(x)$ passes through $A(-2, 8)$ and $B(4, -4)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {-2/-4,1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue] plot[smooth,tension=0.6] coordinates {(-3,5.2) (-2,4) (0,2) (2,0) (4,-2) (5,-3)} node[above right] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (-2.5,4.5) -- (4.5,-2.5);
\fill (-2,4) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (-2,4) {$A(-2,8)$};
\fill (4,-2) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (4,-2) {$B(4,-4)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the average rate of change of $f(x)$ over the interval $[-2, 4]$.

The trajectory of a projectile is graphed with points $P(1, 25)$ and $Q(4, 40)$, where $h$ is height in metres and $t$ is time in seconds.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$h$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue] plot[smooth,tension=0.6] coordinates {(0,0) (1,2.5) (2,4.0) (3,4.5) (4,4.0) (5,2.5) (6,0)} node[above left] {$h(t)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,2.0) -- (5,4.5);
\fill (1,2.5) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (1,2.5) {$P(1,25)$};
\fill (4,4.0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (4,4.0) {$Q(4,40)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Height (m)};
\node[below] at (3.2,-0.9) {Time (s)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the average rate of change in height between $t = 1\text{ s}$ and $t = 4\text{ s}$.
